    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> plantation colony on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guianas">Guiana</a> coast, taken from the English in 1667 and run for a century by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/society-of-suriname">Society of Suriname</a>.</li><li>Enslaved Africans worked its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> estates; runaways formed maroon nations that won peace treaties in the 1760s.</li><li>Indentured Asian migrants made it highly diverse; it became independent in 1975 and has been a democracy since 1991.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-breda-1667">Treaty of Breda</a> of 1667 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> while the English kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a>, which they had renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

